course: dictionary
lesson: 6121
title: Midday
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Midday is the middle of the day. It means twelve o'clock, which is also called noon. «In the morning the Sun is in the east, so shadows point west; at midday in Britain the Sun is in the south, so shadows point north.» Midday is a time you can read on a clock.
explain: Midday can also mean around the middle of the day, and it can describe things too. «A midday meal» is lunch. Look at the words around midday to find out which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Clocks use am and pm to show which half of the day you mean. «To say which half you mean, people add "am" (before midday, from Latin "ante meridiem") or "pm" (after midday, "post meridiem").» When you swap in noon for midday in a sentence, it should still make sense.
fact: Midday is twelve o'clock in the middle of the day, also called noon.
fact: Times before midday use am, and times after midday use pm.
fact: Around midday in summer, the Sun is highest in the sky, so its rays are strongest.
fact: At midday, stay in the shade, wear a hat and use sunscreen, because your shadow is shortest then.
fact: Midnight is twelve hours after midday.
exercise: What time is midday on a clock? | 9 o'clock | 3 o'clock | 6 o'clock | *12 o'clock
exercise: «A midday meal» is another word for which meal? | *Lunch | Bedtime snack | Breakfast
exercise: Liam says «Too late — after noon, you're the fool!» What does that tell you about noon? | It is a time after breakfast | It is a time of night | *It is the same time as midday | It is a type of joke
test: In the morning shadows point west, and at midday in Britain they point north. Which way do shadows point in the evening? | South | North | *East | West
test: Which word means the time after midday? | am | midday | *pm | midnight
exam: Which Latin phrase does "am" come from? | *ante meridiem | midnight hour | post meridiem | meridiem noon
